\section*{Appendix: Additional Derivations and Algorithmic Details}
\subsection*{A. Parameter counts and gate counts}
For $n$ qubits and two rotation layers $[R_y, R_z]$, the parameter count is $P=4n$. The entangler ring uses $n$ CZ gates per layer. Total gate count per forward pass is $k=4n + n$ (single-qubit plus entanglers), ignoring compilation to native pulses.

\subsection*{B. Baseline pseudocode sketches}
Deterministic greedy local search starts from random cuts and iteratively flips single bits if they improve the objective; multiple restarts reduce local minima susceptibility. Simulated annealing performs stochastic bit flips with a cooling schedule accepting unfavorable moves with decreasing probability; both are classical baselines for small graphs.

